2 CONT '''1473 – 1497 [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Bruce-6th-Baron-of-Clackmannan-Rate/303629351820005598?through=6000000001806579012 Sir David Bruce - 6th Baron of Clackmannan]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Received the charter for the lands of Clackmannan and Rait on the event of his father's death in 1473. Knighted by King James IV.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gave eldest son [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-of-Rait/6000000003146136940?through=303629351820005598 Robert] and his wife a charter for the lands of Rait in Perthshire in August 1481. Resigned the charter for Clackmann
2 CONC an in favour of his son David on 11th September 1497. Died around 1506.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barony passed from father to son
2 CONT
2 CONT =='''1497 – 1550 [https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-David-Bruce-7th-Baron-Of-Clackmannan/6000000003435018681  Sir David Bruce - 7th Baron of Clackmannan]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Received the charter for the Lands and Barony of Clackmannan when his father resigned from it in his favour in September 1497. On 1st February 1507 resigned the lands of Rait to his nephew [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Bru
2 CONC ce-of-Rait/6000000003146136955?through=6000000003146136940 
2 CONT David], who in turned resigned his rights to the lands of Clackmannan in favour of his Uncle David Bruce and his family. Sir David's eldest son [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Bruce-of-Clackmannan/6000000003146136970?through=600
2 CONC 0000003435018681 John] died before his father therefore the Barony of Clackmannan passed to John's son.
2 CONT '''
2 CONT Barony passed from grandfather to grandson
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1550 -1609 [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-8th-Bar-of-Clackmanan/6000000003146148174?through=6000000003146136970  Sir Robert Bruce - 8th Baron of Clackmannan]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Due to his father John dying before his grandfather, the Barony passed on to Robert Bruce. His son Norman served as a Colonel in the Army. His son Walter was a servant to Robert Stewart, Commendator of Holyrood and Earl of Orkney 
2 CONC and is believed to have taken part in a confrontation at the Kirk of Kirkwall after which they were charged with the "treasonable taking of the Kirk of Kirkwall".
2 CONT
