1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MASTER EDWARD BRUCE OF BALAIRHALL ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Master Edward Bruce of Blaihall, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-David-Bruce-7th-Baron-Of-Clackmannan/6000000003435018681?through=6000000003615931244 He is identified as: "magrm Edward Bruce filio Da
2 CONC vid Bruce de Clakman militis" in a charter in his favour which was issued by James V, King of Scots, on 20 July 1533. [https://deriv.nls.uk/dcn23/9494/94948513.23.pdf Collections towards a History of the County of Clackmannan, cha
2 CONC rter number 41 on page 15]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Wife==
2 CONT Alison or Cristina Reid See [https://www.geni.com/discussions/271622?msg=1661551 Discussion]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Robert, succeeded his father in Blairhall, and was ancestor of the Bruces of Blairhall, and the Bruces, Baronets of Kinross and Balcaskie. Both these families are extinct in the male line.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Edward, first Lord Bruce of Kinloss, of whom presently .
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Sir George, of Carnock, ancestor of the Earls of Elgin and Kincardine. (See next article.)
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. William, of Cothill and Collestoune, in Aberdeenshire. He is said to have been first a priest4 in Kinloss Abbey, but signs as a witness various documents connected with Kinloss as ' brother - german and factor to my Lord Abbot 
2 CONC of Kinloss.' He died s. p. before 24 May 1609, on which date his nephew Edward Bruce, afterwards second Lord Bruce of Kinloss,5 was served heir to him.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Margaret.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Bessie,1 married David Bar.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03paul/page/474/mode/1up?view=theater&q=blairhall p474
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 July 1533: Charter of Protection, by King James V., to Mr Edward Bruce, son of Sir David Bruce of Clackmannan, knight,. [https://deriv.nls.uk/dcn23/9494/94948513.23.pdf Collections towards a History of the County of Clackman
2 CONC nan, charter number 41 on page 15]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 April 1537: Charter by Robert Brady of Easter Kennet, to Mr Edward Bruce and his heirs and assignees, of three parts of his (the said John Brady's) lands of Easter Kennet, lying in the County of Clackmannan, also his croft l
2 CONC ying in the territory and liberty of the town of Clackmannan, on the west side of the church thereof, and situate between the lands of David Bruce of Clackmannan in the east and west - item two parts of a Tenement of land called B
2 CONC axters land - Croft of land called the Crooked croft, bounded by the high road on the east, and the lands of the foresaid David Bruce on the west, also two parts of the said Crooked croft and bounded as said is - annualrent of 40 
2 CONC pence money of Scotland, payable from the lands of John Arhle lying in the town of Clackmannan - annualrent of 10 shillings payable from the lands of Gilbert Coulsone lying on the north side of the town of Clackmannan, and annualr
2 CONC ent of 20 shillings, payable from the lands of John Smith, lying as said is; and that in consideration of a certain sum of money paid to him by the foresaid David Bruce, in his urgent necessity - To be holden, the foresaid lands a
2 CONC nd annualrents, with the right of pasturage on the Commonty of Clackmannan used and wont by the said Edward Bruce, his heirs and assignees, of the King and his successors, in fee & heritage, for services used and wont, and service
2 CONC s to the Courts of Clackmannan - Dated at Edinburgh. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD11%2f42&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Edward+Bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records o
2 CONC f Scotland, Papers of the Bruce Family of Kennet, Clackmannanshire. reference GD11/42]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: An abstract of this charter was printed in [https://deriv.nls.uk/dcn23/9494/94948513.23.pdf Collections towards a History of the County of Clackmannan. See charter number 37 on page 9]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1544: Charter by the said Commendator and Abbot in favour of the said Edward Brus [Bruce] and his spouse, Cristina Reid, of the said lands of Bargady and others. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.a
2 CONC spx?reference=RH6%2f1337&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cristina+reid&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register House charters, 1st series, reference RH6/1337]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1544: Precept of sasine by the said Commendator and Abbot for infefting the said Edward Brus [Bruce] and Cristina Reid in the said lands and others. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference
2 CONC =RH6%2f1338&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cristina+reid&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register House charters, 1st series, reference RH6/1338]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 November 1546: Precept of sasine by the said Commendator and Abbot for infefting the said Edward Bruse [Bruce] and Cristina Reid in the lands of Corstoun in the lordship of Culros [Culross] and sheriffdom of Perth. [https://
2 CONC catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f1391A&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cristina+reid&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register House charters, 1st series, reference RH6/
2 CONC 1391A]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 December 1546: Discharge by William, commendator of culross, [comptroller] for £8 13s.4d. for the burgh maills and small customs of Cupar. Witnesses: master Edward Bruce Alexander Gaw, William Colvile and sir John Broun, chap
2 CONC lain. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=B13%2f22%2f20&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=master+edward+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Records of Cupar Burgh, refe
2 CONC rence B13/22/20]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 December 1552: Charter by William, Commendator of Culross, with consent of Robert, Bishop of Orkney and Abbot of Kinlos [Kinloss], in favour of Edward Bruce of Estir Kennett and Cristina Reid his spouse of the lands of Barga
2 CONC dye and others. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f1572&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cristina+reid&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register House charters, 1s
2 CONC t series, reference RH6/1572]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 May 1564: Precept of clare constat by William, Commendator of Culros [Culross], for infefting Robert Bruce as heir of his father, Master Edward Bruce of Estir Kennet, in the lands of Bargadye and others. [https://catalogue.n
2 CONC rscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f1951&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=master+edward+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register House charters, 1st series, reference RH6/1951]'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 February 1566-67: Precept of Clare Constat by Master Jerome Chene, archdean of Zetland and rector of parish church of Torrie, in favour of Robert Bruce as heir to deceased Master Edward Bruce of Eister Bennet [sic], in church
2 CONC  lands and glebe of parish church of Torrie. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD15%2f849&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=master+edward+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Sc
2 CONC otland, Erskine family of Cardross, Perthshire, reference GD15/849]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    10
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 October 1569: Procuratory of resignation by Mr Jerome Chene [Cheyne], Archdeacon of Zetland, parson and vicar of Torry, in the diocese of Sanctandrois [Saint Andrews] and sheriffdom of Fife, to resign the parsonage and vicara
2 CONC ge of Torry into the hands of the King in favour of Edward Bruce son of deceased Mr Edward Bruce of Eister Kennit [Easter Kennet]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD56%2f33&st=1&tc=y&
2 CONC tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Edward+Bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1566&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Rollo family of Duncrub, Perthshire, reference GD56/33]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    11
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 July 1574: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms a charter dated 12 September 1559 which had been issued by Walter, Abbot of Kinloss. The charter in question confirmed that the Ab
2 CONC bot had set in feu-ferme to (quondam) Master Edward Bruce of Easter Kennet the lands of Killesmond and others in the barony of Strathisla, Regality of Kinloss and Sheriffdom of Banff. The King also confirmed a charter dated 3 Marc
2 CONC h 1573 by which Robert Bruce of Easter Kennet, son and heir of Master Edward Bruce of Easter Kennet conveyed part of this land to James Dempstar of Auchterles. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/602/mode/1up 
2 CONC RMS 1546-80: charter number 2268]'''
2 CONT
