2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://www.thepeerage.com/p17983.htm#i179823 Biographical Summary by Darryl Lundy's Peerage] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Edward Bruce of Blairhall was born in 1505. He was the son of Sir David Bruce of Clackmannan and Janet Blackadder. He married Alison Reid, daughter of William Reid. He died in 1565. In 1537 he had charter of Easter Kennet. 
2 CONC In 1540 he had charter of Bergandy and 2/3rds of Shirresmith, from William, commendator of Culross. In 1541 he bought Blairhall. He lived at Blairhall, Clackmannanshire, Scotland. Children of Sir Edward Bruce of Blairhall and Alis
2 CONC on Reid (1) Robert Bruce (2)  Sir George Bruce d. 6 May 1625 (3) William Bruce d. 1609 (5) Edward Bruce, 1st Baron Bruce of Kinlosse b. 1548, d. 14 Jan 1610/11 [http://www.thepeerage.com/p17983.htm#i179823 Darryl Lundy's Peerage]'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =='''BRUCE,  EARLS  OF  ELGIN  AND AILESBURY''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03paul/page/466/mode/1up?view=theater Balfour Paul, James, ed. (1906). The Scots Peerage, Vol. III. Edinburgh: David Douglas. pp. 467–468. ISBN 0-9711966-2-1.]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-David-Bruce-7th-Baron-Of-Clackmannan/6000000003435018681?through=303629351820005598 Sir  David  Bruce],  eldest  son  of  the  second  marriage, succeeded  his  father  in  Clackmannan,  to  the  e
2 CONC xclusion  of his  elder  half-brother  [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-of-Rait/6000000003146136940?through=303629351820005598 Robert]  and  his  son  [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Bruce-of-Rait/6000000003146136955?t
2 CONC hrough=6000000003146136940 David].  On  11 September  1497  he  had  a  Crown  charter of  Clackmannan, subject   to   his   father's  liferent  and   that   of   his   mother [https://www.geni.com/people/Mariot-Herries/6000000001
2 CONC 806317482?through=6000000003435018681 Mariota  Herries].  On  3  February  1506-7  he  had  a  Crown charter erecting  Clackmannan,  with  other  lands,  into  a barony,  when  he  is  styled  '  David  Bruis  de  Clackmannan mile
2 CONC s,  Alius  quondam  David  Bruce  de  Clackmannan,'  his nephew,  [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Bruce-of-Rait/6000000003146136955?through=6000000003146136940 David  Bruce  of  Rait],  having  resigned  any  interest he  might
2 CONC   have  in  it.  The  estate  must  have  been  a  very large  one,  from  the  enumeration  of  the  lands  incorporated in  the  barony.  He  had  a  licence  to  hold  a  fair  at  Clackmannan on  the  Feast  of  St.  Bartholom
2 CONC ew  annually,  18  April 1517,  which  was  confirmed 18  September  1542.  Sir  David  was on  an  assize 1  December  1554,  On  21  January  1550-51  he gave  a  charter   to  [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-8th-Bar-o
2 CONC f-Clackmanan/6000000003146148174  Robert  Bruce],  his  grandson  and  apparent heir,  and  [https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Livingston/6000000011335665999?through=6000000003146148174 Janet  Levingstone],  his  wife,  of  an  an
2 CONC nualrent  of forty  merks,  and  was  alive  12  June  1556,  when  he  gave a  precept  of  sasine  for  infefting  Robert  Bruce,  brother- german  of  the  deceased  Mr.  John  Bruce,  in  the  lands  of Wester  Kennet.  [https
2 CONC ://www.geni.com/people/Sir-David-Bruce-7th-Baron-Of-Clackmannan/6000000003435018681?through=303610207620004050 Sir  David]  married  [https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Bruce-Baroness-of-O-Lack/303610207620004050?through=6000000003
2 CONC 435018681 Jean],  daughter  of  [https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Patrick-Blackadder-of-Tulliallan/303623670910007050?through=303610207620004050 Sir Patrick  Blacadder  of  Tulliallan],  by  whom  he  had  issue  five sons  and  fo
2 CONC ur  daughters,  viz. : —
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.[https://www.geni.com/people/John-Bruce-of-Clackmannan/6000000003146136970?through=6000000003435018681 John],  died  vita  patris  before  14  February  1550-51,  but carried  on  the  line  of  the  Clackmannan  family,  which 
2 CONC became  extinct  in  the  male  line  on  the  death,  8  July 1772,  of  Henry  Bruce,  fifteenth  and  last  Baron.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. ''' [https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Edward-Bruce-of-Blairhall-and-Easter-Kennet/6000000003615931244?through=6000000003435018681 Edward,  of  Blairhall]  born  1505,   had  a  charter  of  the  lands  of Easter  Kennet,  1537, 
2 CONC  on  the  resignation  of  Robert  Brady. This  charter  was  confirmed11  by  James  v.  24  April  1537. He  had  also  a  charter 12  from  the  Abbot  of  Culross  7  June 1540,  confirmed  15  February  1542-43,  of  the  lan
2 CONC ds  of  Bergady and  two  parts  of  the  Shire  mills
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Bruce-III/6000000003435071438?through=6000000003435018681 David,  of  Green].    He  was  ancestor  of  the  Bruces  of Kennet,  Lords  Balfour  of  Burleigh.  (See  vol.  i. p.  547.)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.  [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-of-Lynmiln/6000000180661927996?through=6000000003435018681 Robert,  of  Lynmylne.]    The  Swedish  Bruces  ennobled in  1668  were  probably  descended  from  him.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.  [https://www.geni.com/people/Patrick-Bruce-of-Valleyfield/6000000014194986036 Patrick,  of  Valleyfield].    He  had  a  charter  of  Valley-field  from  the  Commendator  of  Culross,  8  June  1540,  to himself  and  Margare
2 CONC t  Falconer,  his  wife,  which  was confirmed7  15  February  1542-43.  In  this  confirmation charter  he  is  called  son  of  Sir  David  Bruce  of Clackmannan,  Knight.  He  is  said  to  have  resigned the  lands  and  baron
2 CONC y  of  Valleyfield  to  James  Preston of   Craigmillar,  and  to  have  died   s.  p.,  leaving  the estate  of  Green  to  his  brother  David  ;  but,  on  the other  hand,  David  appears  as  a  witness  to  a  charter under 
2 CONC  the  designation  'of  '  de  Greyne,'  30  January 1536-37.  He  is  also  a  witness   to  a  precept  of  sasine 6  November  1536,  and  in  an  ancient  MS.  pedigree, endorsed  1640,  Patrick  is  styled   of  Valleyfield,'
2 CONC   and David  is  called  '  of  Greyne.'  It  would,  on  the  whole, seem  that  Patrick  never  possessed  Green,  but  only Valleyfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.  [https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Bruce/6000000009380158593?through=6000000003146136970 Elizabeth],  married,  first,  to  Alexander  Dundas  of  Fingask ;   they  had  a  charter  of  Cottis, 8  August 1542.  She  was  m
2 CONC arried,  secondly,  to  Robert  Oolless of  Bonneymoon.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.  [https://www.geni.com/people/Marion-Bruce/6000000193466079848 Marion],  married,  first,  about  1500,  to  John  Menteith  of Caverkay ;  secondly,  to  Robert  Bruce  of  Airth  ; and  thirdly,  to  Magnus  Sinclair  of  Kyn
2 CONC ninmonth, second  son 7  of  William,  Lord  Sinclair.  She  died  July 1575;  will  dated  at  Dysart  18  June  1575,  confirmed 11  August  1575.8
2 CONT
2 CONT 8.  [https://www.geni.com/people/Agnes-Bruce/6000000003645966321?through=6000000009380158593 Agnes],  married  to  John  Elphinstone,  parson  of  Invernochty,  with  issue.
