1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MARION BRUCE Lady Airth ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marion Bruce, here treated, is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-David-Bruce-7th-Baron-Of-Clackmannan/6000000003435018681?through=6000000193466079848 [https://archive.org/details/brucesofairththe00arms/page/n46/mo
2 CONC de/1up The Bruces of Airth and their Cadets: 14]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marion Bruce, here treated, died in July 1575. She probably died at Dysart in Fife, Scotland, where she made her last will and testament on 15 June 1575.  [NRS:  CC8/8/3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marion Bruce, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-of-Airth/6000000002006454467?through=6000000193466079848 They were granted a papal dispensation for their marriage on 23 March 529.  [http://catalogue
2 CONC .nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD37%2f358&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+schaw&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD37/358]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marion Bruce, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Magnus-Sinclair-of-Kynninmonth/6000000193466545830?through=6000000193466079848 They are noticed as man and wife on 14 November 1561. [https://archive.org/details/r
2 CONC egistrummagnisi04scot/page/318/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 1402]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Her Last Will and Testament ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marion Bruce, Lady Airth, the wife of Magnus Sinclair of Kynninmonth, made her last will and testament on 18 June 1575. It was made in the Burgh of Dysart in Fife. She nominated and constituted her husband https://www.geni.com/
2 CONC people/Magnus-Sinclair-of-Kynninmonth/6000000193466545830?through=6000000193466079848 and her second son https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-of-Baldrig/6000000199157960835 to be her only executors and intromitters with her wh
2 CONC ole goods and gear. Confirmation was granted to the executors on 11 August 1575. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Marioun Bruce, Lady Airth, sometime spouse to M
2 CONC agnus Sinclair in Kynninmonth, reference CC8/8/3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000199242855821 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000199236313866 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000199236236845 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000199236432821 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[23 March 1529]: Dispensation in form of apostolic letters by Antonius, cardinal of the Four Crowned Saints, in favour of Robert Bruce of Artht and Marion [or Marjorie] Bruce, for their marriage, in spite of fact that they are 
2 CONC related in third and fourth degrees of affinity, by her relationship to Margaret Schaw who has known said Robert carnally. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD37%2f358&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=
2 CONC n&tp=n&k=margaret+schaw&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Bruce family of Airth, reference GD37/358]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 July 1547: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland which confirmed possession of two bovates of the land of Airth, and other lands, to Alexander Bruce and his wife Jonete Levingstoun. Alexander is identified as the son and a
2 CONC pparent heir of Robert Bruce of Airth, who had previously resigned these lands in favour of his son. Robert Bruce of Airth reserved his own liferent and that of his wife Mariote Bruce. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi
2 CONC 04scot/page/29/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 118]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 November 1561: Charter by which Robert Scot, portioner of Kynnynmonth, confirms that he has sold part of his lands of Kynnynmonth to Magnus Sinclair, son of William, Lord Sinclair, and his wife Mariote Bruce. This charter wa
2 CONC s confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 6 December 1561. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/318/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 1402]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 May 1564: Instrument of redemption by Robert Drummond of Carnok, knight, of a seventh part of the lands of Carnok on payment to Marion Bruce, Lady Airthe, and Mawnis Sinclare, now her spouse, of the sum of 567 merks 6s. 8d.,
2 CONC  the said Marion discharging the said Robert of all bygone rents and that in respect Alexander Bruce of Airthe had become obliged to pay 60 merks to Margaret Bruce, daughter of the said Marion as for complete payment of all bygone
2 CONC  dues, the said Marion also renouncing and discharging a contract between her and the said Robert, dated 3 March, 1557, by which the said Robert bound himself to pay 100 merks to Alexander Bruce of Airthe and the said Marion. Date
2 CONC d 19 May, 1564. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD17%2f153&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1575&di=n National Records of Scotland, Title deeds relating to 
2 CONC the lands of Carnock and Plean, reference GD17/153]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In dorso: Discharge by Alexander Bruce of Airthe in favour of Sir Robert Drummond of Carnok, knight, of the sum of 240 merks for which the said Alexander had been bound as cautioner to the said Robert, for bygone dues of the sa
2 CONC id lands. Dated 20 Nov., 1565.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Attached is discharge by Marion Bruce, Magnus Sinclar, son of William, Lord Synclar, her spouse, and Margaret Bruce, her daughter, in favour of the said Robert Drummond of the sum of 120 merks in complete payment of sum of 240 
2 CONC merks due as bygone duties of above lands. Dated 5 Nov., 1565.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 January 1573: Bond of Reversion by Magnus Synclar [Sinclair] of Kyninmonthe [Kinninmonth] and Marion Bruiss [Bruce], his spouse, to John Maluyll [Melville] of Rayth [Raith], of annualrent of £20 Scots from lands of Rayth, on 
2 CONC payment of 300 merks. [2 seals appended.] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f301&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=kinninmonth&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1575&di=n National Records of S
2 CONC cotland, Papers of the Leslie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/3/301]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 June 1576: Extract bond of caution by Henry, Lord Sinclair, as cautioner for Magnus Sinclair of Kynninmonth [Kinninmonth], to Andrew Bruce, son of umquhile Marion Bruce, spouse of said Magnus, of money received by Magnus on t
2 CONC he reversion to James Gib [Gibb] of Ballinkirk of sixteen part lands of Over Stintoun [Over Stenton] in regality of Dunfermline and sheriffdom of Fife and reversion to Thomas Scott of Abbotshall of annualrent on lands of Abbotshal
2 CONC l. Registered: B of C and S, 18 June 1576. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD164%2f8&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=andrew+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland
2 CONC , Papers of the Sinclair Family, Earls of Rosslyn, reference GD164/8]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence cited in the Bruces of Airth and their Cadets ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 May 1548:  Charter by Robert Bruce of Airth to Robert Bruce, his son and apparent heir, and Jonet Livingston his spouse, of the Mill of Airth, reserving Robert's liferent, and a terce to " Mariote Bruce spouse mee moderne." 
2 CONC At Airth, Witnesses, Mr. Thomas Bruys, James Brus, etc. [https://archive.org/details/brucesofairththe00arms/page/n380/mode/1up The Bruces of Airth: xxxiii]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
