1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == DAVID BRUCE OF CLACKMANNAN elder ==
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''David Bruce of Clackmannan, here treated, died before 2 December 1502. . [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=inu.30000047784453&view=1up&seq=608 Acts of the Lords of Council in Civil Causes II: 456]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/L6M2-RSW
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bruce-389
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 November 1490: Charter by which David Bruce of Clackmannan, lord of the barony of Rate, confirms that he has given certain land in the barony of Rate to the Abbot and convent of the Monastery of Scone. The land in question l
2 CONC ay adjacent to the land which formerly belonged to his deceased son Robert Bruce, and then to Robert's wife Elizabeth Lindsay. David Bruce made this gift  for the benefit of his own soul and that of his wife MARIOT HERIS. His char
2 CONC ter was witnessed by his son Alexander Bruce and others. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/426/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 2031]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 September 1497: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by Which James IV, King of Scots, confirms possession of the barony of Clackmannan in the sheriffdom of Clackmannan, and the barony of Rate in the sheriffdom of Perth,
2 CONC  to David Bruce, son of David Bruce of Clackmannan, and his heirs. Clackmannan and Rate had previously been resigned by David senior in order to obtain a new grant in favour of David junior and his heirs. David senior reserved his
2 CONC  own liferent and that of his wife MARIOTE HERRIS. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/505/mode/1up  RMS1424-1513: charter number 2372]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 December 1502: Bruce of Clakmannan. Menteith of Caverea. Contract of marriage. Failure to procure dispensation. Action by David Bruse, younger of Clakmannane, against John Menteith of Caverca “for the wrangas postponing and d
2 CONC iffering til raise and bring hame ane dispesacione fra the Court of Rome for the completing and solempnyng of lauchfull matrimone betuex sade Jhone and Marione Bruse, dochter to the sade David Bruse, elder, and sister to David Bru
2 CONC se, younger,eftir the forme of the indenturis.” The pursuer compearing by Edward and Robert the Bruse, his procurators, and the defender personally, the Lords ordain the said John to deliver to the said David “the authentic copy u
2 CONC nder the transsumpt of the sade Marione conjunct feftment of the sadis landis of Caverca, togidder with the rentalling of the takkis of the landis of Dalgrane. The Colzare Raw myln, Petbaithle, with the auchtene part of Maistertou
2 CONC ne, for als mony termes and yeris as he has of the  sammyn and prodicit before the Lordis; and als decretis and deliveris the sade Jhone til be qwyt of the clame of five hundreith merkis clamyt be umquhile David Bruse, elder of Cl
2 CONC akmannan. And David Bruse, yonger, for their costis , dampnage and expensis, because he failyeit til mak resignation of his landis and til bring hame the sade dispensacion, sen that the sade Jhone of Menteith has producit and lauc
2 CONC hfull resignacione and conjunct, feftment. Dispensacione and ane sufficient rentaling of the sade Marione in presens of the sadid Lordis.” [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=inu.30000047784453&view=1up&seq=608 Acts of the Lor
2 CONC ds of Council in Civil Causes II: 456]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 December 1502: Same dept. Action by John Menteith of Kaverky against David Bruse, elder, and David Brus, younger of Clakmannan, for 40 l, Scots. The pursuer compearing personally, and David Bruse, younger, compearing by Edwar
2 CONC d and Robert the Bruse, his procurators, the Lords ordain the said David Bruse, younger to pay thesaid sum to the pursuer in terms of his obligation produced. [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=inu.30000047784453&view=1up&seq
2 CONC =608 Acts of the Lords of Council in Civil Causes II: 456]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
