2 CONT =='''BRUCE,  EARLS  OF  ELGIN  AND AILESBURY''' [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03paul/page/466/mode/1up?view=theater Balfour Paul, James, ed. (1906). The Scots Peerage, Vol. III. Edinburgh: David Douglas. pp. 467–468
2 CONC . ISBN 0-9711966-2-1.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Bruce-6th-Baron-of-Clackmannan-Rate/303629351820005598?through=6000000001806579012 Sir  David  Bruce],  the  elder  son,  succeeded  his  father  in Clackmannan.    He  had   a   charter  as   ab
2 CONC ove    from   King James  in.,  proceeding  upon  his  father's  resignation  of  the lands  of  Clackmannan  and  Rait,  etc.    He  was  knighted  by James  IV.,  with  whom  he    was  in  great  favour.     On  28 August  1481
2 CONC   he  settled  the  estate  of   Rait  in  Perthshire on  Robert  Bruce,   his  eldest  son  and  apparent  heir,  and Elizabeth  Lindsay,  his  wife.    This  charter  was  confirmed by  James  IV 15  December  1488.    He  marri
2 CONC ed,  first,  [https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Stirling/6000000003146148185?through=303629351820005598 Janet], daughter  of  Sir  William  Stirling  of  Keir,  by  whom  he  had one  son : — 
2 CONT 1.  Robert  Bruce  of  Rait.     For  some    unknown  reason (probably  the  influence  of  his  step-mother)  he  was passed  over  by  his  father  in  the  succession  to  Clack- mannan,    in    favour     of     his     half
2 CONC -brother    David. Robert    of    Rait    died     vita     patris     before    1490,when  his  widow '  was  wife  of  Alexander  Scott, son  of  William  Scott  of  Balwery,  and  in  a  charter from  his  father  Sir  David  
2 CONC to  the  monastery  of  Scone, 29  November  1490,  he  is  mentioned  as  'quondam.' This  charter  was  confirmed 2  7  May  1491.  He  married, about  1484,  Elizabeth  Lindsay,  and  by  her  had  issue two  sons,  viz. : —
2 CONT (1)  David,  succeeded  in  Rait.
2 CONT (2)  Alexander,3  tutor  to  James,  his  brother's  son,  in  1522. This  family  of  Rait  and  Fingask  has  been  traced  down  to 1679 ;  the  estate  of  Fingask  was  sold  in  1672 4  to  the  Threipland family. It  is  by
2 CONC   no  means  certain  that  there  are  no  male  descendants of  this  branch ;  if  so,  the  eldest  of  them  would  undoubtedly be  head  of  the  whole  family  of  Bruce.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir  David  married,  secondly,  [https://www.geni.com/people/Mariot-Herries/6000000001806317482?through=303629351820005598 Mariota],  daughter  of  John Herries  of  Terregles,  and  widow  of  Sir  David  Stewart of  Rosyth.  In
2 CONC   a  Grown  charter  of  his  estate  of  Clackmannan in  favour  of  his  son  David,  a  life-rent  is  reserved to  himself  and  Dame  Mariota  Herries,  his  spouse,  of  date 11  September  1497. He  died  about  1500,  leav
2 CONC ing  issue  by his  second  wife  two  sons  and  two  daughters,  viz. : —
2 CONT 2.  Sir  David,  succeeded  in  Clackmannan.
2 CONT 3.  Alexander,  witnessed   the  charter   of   29   November 1490  mentioned  above.
2 CONT 4.  Margaret,  mentioned   in  a  deed,  1477.
2 CONT 5.  Christian,  married  to  Sir  James  Shaw  of  Sauchie. 
2 CONT Sir  David   is   said  to  have  had  two  more  sons   by  his second  wife,  ancestors  respectively  of  the  Bruces  of  Ham and  Standstill,  Caithness.
