1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =[https://www.clackmannanshire.scot/index.php/history/barony-of-clackmannan The Barony of Clackmannan]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1497 – 1550 [https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-David-Bruce-7th-Baron-Of-Clackmannan/6000000003435018681  Sir David Bruce - 7th Baron of Clackmannan]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Received the charter for the Lands and Barony of Clackmannan when his father resigned from it in his favour in September 1497. On 1st February 1507 resigned the lands of Rait to his nephew [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Bruce-
2 CONC of-Rait/6000000003146136955?through=6000000003146136940 
2 CONT David], who in turned resigned his rights to the lands of Clackmannan in favour of his Uncle David Bruce and his family. Sir David's eldest son [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Bruce-of-Clackmannan/6000000003146136970?through=600
2 CONC 0000003435018681 John] died before his father therefore the Barony of Clackmannan passed to John's son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barony passed from grandfather to grandson
2 CONT
2 CONT =='''1550 -1609 [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-8th-Bar-of-Clackmanan/6000000003146148174?through=6000000003146136970  Sir Robert Bruce - 8th Baron of Clackmannan]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Due to his father John dying before his grandfather, the Barony passed on to Robert Bruce. His son Norman served as a Colonel in the Army. His son Walter was a servant to Robert Stewart, Commendator of Holyrood and Earl of Orkn
2 CONC ey and is believed to have taken part in a confrontation at the Kirk of Kirkwall after which they were charged with the "treasonable taking of the Kirk of Kirkwall".'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Barony passed from father to son
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1609 – 1642 Sir Robert Bruce - 9th Baron of Clackmannan'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Inherited the Barony of Clackmannan after the death of his father. Died around 1642.
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.brucefamily.com/lineage.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 1550 Sir Robert Bruce, 8th Baron of Clackmannan m. Janet Livingston. He had two sons that I know of Robert and Henry, and maybe a George Bruce of Harperland.
2 CONT
