2 CONT <blockquote>'''The Question of Identity'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''According to the late Major William Bruce Armstrong, https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Edward-Bruce-of-Blairhall-and-Easter-Kennet/6000000003615931244?through=6000000008947212350 married a lady named Alison Reid, said
2 CONC  by him to have been the: "daughter of John Reid of Aikenhead, and sister of Robert Reid, Bishop of Orkney." [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/476/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II
2 CONC I: 476] By way of proof, but without explanation, he cited Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland which identifies a different father for Sir Edward's wife:  "Alison, daughter of William Reid of Aikenhead, Esq., in vicecomitatu de C
2 CONC lackmannan, and sister of Robert Reid, Bishop of Orkney." [https://archive.org/details/bim_eighteenth-century_the-peerage-of-scotland-_douglas-sir-robert-bar_1764/page/235/mode/1up Douglas Peerage: 235] Neither man cites documenta
2 CONC ry evidence of the given name of Sir Edward's wife, and their claims are not supported by surviving records.'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
