2 CONT *''''''Edward Bruce, 1st Baron Bruce of Kinlosse1
2 CONT *''''''M, #10994, b. 1548, d. 14 January 1610/11
2 CONT *Last Edited=18 Jun 2011
2 CONT *''''''    Edward Bruce, 1st Baron Bruce of Kinlosse was born in 1548.1 He was the son of Sir Edward Bruce of Blairhall and Alison Reid.1 He married Magdalene Clerk, daughter of Alexander Clerk.3 He died on 14 January 1610/11.3 He
2 CONC  was buried at Rolls Chapel, Chancery Lane, London, England.3 His will was probated on 14 January 1610/11.3
2 CONT *''''''     He was admitted to Scottish Bar.1 He was Commissary of Edinburgh in 1583.1 He held the office of Lord of Session between 1597 and 1604.1 He held the office of Ambassador to England in 1600, and was instrumental in ensu
2 CONC ring the succesion of King James VI to the English throne.3 He was created 1st Lord Kinloss [Scotland] on 2 February 1601/2.1 He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) on 4 May 1603.1 He held the office of Master of the Rolls f
2 CONC rom 4 May 1603 to 14 January 1610/11.1 He was created 1st Baron Bruce of Kinlosse [Scotland] on 8 July 1604, with remainder to his male heirs.3 He was awarded the honorary degree of Master of Arts (M.A.) by Oxford University, Oxfo
2 CONC rd, Oxfordshire, England, in 1605.1 He was created 1st Lord Bruce of Kinloss [Scotland] on 3 May 1608, with remainder to any of his heirs.3 His last will was dated 9 August 1610. He has an extensive biographical entry in the Dicti
2 CONC onary of National Biography.4
2 CONT *''''''Child of Edward Bruce, 1st Baron Bruce of Kinlosse
