2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Fake Genealogy'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''According to the Bruce Y-DNA Project, Sir George Bruce of Carnock, here treated, is the son of Sir Robert Bruce of Blairhall and Easter Kennet (1532-1617) and his wife Lady Margaret Hamilton (floruit 15351619). He i
2 CONC s said by the Project to have been born in 1551 and to have died on 6 May 1625. [https://www.familytreedna.com/groups/bruce/about/goals Bruce Surname Y-DNA Project: Group 37-M269 IN84933] This is contradicted by the Scots Peerage 
2 CONC account of the family, which identifies him as the third son of Edward Bruce, first of Blairhall and Easter Kennet. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/n503/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 503] The Bruce Y
2 CONC -DNA Project does not offer ant supporting evidence for  it's proposition, but the Scots Peerage account is supported by a charter made in favour of Henry Baverage, notary, and his future wife Jonet Hodge, wherein the names of Geo
2 CONC rge Bruce and his older brother, Robert Bruce of Blairhall, are noticed in the witness list.  [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/367/mode/1up RMS 1580-93: charter number 1110] Any doubts about the identity of
2 CONC  the younger brother of Robert Bruce of Blairhall are dispelled by a deed of discharge which was issued by him after his elevation to the knighthood. In this deed he is identified as Sir George Bruce of Carnox, brother of the late
2 CONC  Edward, Lord Bruce, Master of the Rolls.. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD421%2f3%2f26&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1625&di=y NRS: GD421/3/26]'''</bl
2 CONC ockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Question of Identity ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to the late Major William Bruce Armstrong, writing in his account of the Bruce Earls of Elgin and Kincardine for The Scots Peerage, Sir George Bruce of Carnock, here treated, is the third son of https://www.geni.com/p
2 CONC eople/Sir-Edward-Bruce-of-Blairhall-and-Easter-Kennet/6000000003615931244?through=6000000009437191685 and the brother of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-of-Blairhall-Easter-Kennet/6000000017845337880?through=6000000009437
2 CONC 191685 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/n503/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 484] He is noticed in company with his brother on 17 June 1582. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/367/
2 CONC mode/1up RMS 1580-93: charter number 1110]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Brother of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-of-Blairhall-Easter-Kennet/6000000017845337880?through=6000000009437191685 ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir George Bruce of Carnock, here treated, is noticed as the brother of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-of-Blairhall-Easter-Kennet/6000000017845337880?through=6000000009437191685 on 17 June 1582. [https://archive.org/d
2 CONC etails/registrummagnisi05scot/page/367/mode/1up RMS 1580-93: charter number 1110]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Brother of https://www.geni.com/people/Edward-Bruce-1st-Lord-Kinloss/6000000008946396034?through=6000000009437191685 ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir George Bruce of Carnock, here treated, is noticed as the brother of https://www.geni.com/people/Edward-Bruce-1st-Lord-Kinloss/6000000008946396034?through=6000000009437191685 on 20 November 1614,  [https://catalogue.nrscotla
2 CONC nd.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD421%2f3%2f26&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1625&di=y NRS: GD421/3/26] and again on 9 June 1622. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06sco
2 CONC t/page/605/mode/1up RMS 1593-1608: charter number 1671]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir George Bruce of Carnock, here treated, is reported to have died on 6 May 1625.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==  Burial ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir George Bruce of Carnock was buried on 12 May 1625. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f39%2f35%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Sir+George+Bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS
2 CONC : GD112/39/35/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir George Bruce of Carnock, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Euphame-Primrose/6000000006444553947?through=6000000009437191685 A date for the marriage has not been identified, bit she was his wife when she died
2 CONC  on 13 October 1609. [NRS: CC6/5/3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir George Bruce of Carnock, here treated, is reported to have had eight children, three son and five daughter. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/485/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 485]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/George-Bruce-of-Carnock/6000000013754779555?through=6000000009437191685 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Bruce-of-Alva/6000000014326152080?through=6000000009437191685 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-Lord-Broomhall/6000000011335997696?through=6000000009437191685 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Anne-Bruce/6000000014326075404?through=6000000009437191685 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Magdelene-Bruce/6000000022501687588?through=6000000009437191685 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Christian-Bruce/6000000014325537745?through=6000000009437191685 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Nicolas-Bruce-Lady-Braid/6000000014325984201?through=6000000009437191685 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Bruce/6000000004993828083?through=6000000009437191685 '''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir George Bruce of Carnock, here treated, appears to have had a sixth daughter named Elizabeth, either that or her name has been confused with one of the other daughters whose names appear to have been omitted from the testame
2 CONC nt dative of https://www.geni.com/people/Euphame-Primrose/6000000006444553947?through=6000000009437191685 For example, Anne Bruce, Christian Bruce, or Margaret Bruce.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Bruce/6000000194056352827?through=6000000009437191685 '''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Testament Dative and Inventory of his wife Euphame Primrose ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Euphame Primrose died intestate on 13 October 1609. On 31 March 1612 her Testament Dative and Inventory was given up by her widowed husband, Sir George Bruce of Carnock. It was given up in name and behalf of  five of their chil
2 CONC dren, that is Alexander Bruce, Robert Bruce, Magdalane Bruce, Elizabeth Bruce and Nicolas Bruce, who were recognised as executors dative to their deceased mother by the Commissary Court of Dunblane. Confirmation was granted to the
2 CONC  executors dative on 31 March 1612. [National Records of Scotland, Dunblane Commissary Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of Euphame Prymrois, spouse to Sir George Bruce of Carnock, knight, reference CC6/5/3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000193687333838 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000193686741887 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000193686933851 Image of Testament]
2 CONT
