2 CONC =1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1625&di=n National Records of Scotland, Erskine family of Cardross, Perthshire, reference GD15/107]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     31
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 May 1625: Letter from Mr D Prymrois, Crawmond, to Sir Duncan Campbell of Glenurquhy, kt. . . . . . As for my comming to your m[astership] I sould not spare my paiunes gif it wer to go to Venice for your pleasure, Bot now Sir
2 CONC  George Bruce in Culross is departed this lyfe, and we wilbe at his buriall upon the twelt of this instant, quher I sall have occasion to meit with William Murray ... and get inspection of these wreats whiche he hes in his wyfs cu
2 CONC stodie, and sall do quhat I can to setle him'; will come if necessary and asks Glenorchy to send a boy.
2 CONT Postscript intimating enclosure of writer's verses on the king's death and an epitaph on late marquess of Hamilton. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f39%2f35%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&
2 CONC tn=n&tp=n&k=Sir+George+Bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), Correspondence, reference GD112/39/35/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    32
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 July 1625: GEORGIUS BRUCE de Carnock, haeres Domini Georgii Bruce de Carnock, militis, patris. ix. 62. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPS
2 CONC I5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=snippet&q=bruce&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum etc. II]  See also [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue
2 CONC /details.aspx?reference=GD15%2f542&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1625&di=y NRS: GD15/542]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    33
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 July 1625: GEORGIUS BRUCE de Carnock, haeres Domini Georgii Bruce de Carnock, militis, patris. ix. 90. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPS
