2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1587: Tack by Walter, abbot of Kinlos [Kinloss], and the convent thereof to William Bruce, brother of Robert Bruce of Blairhall, of the teinds of half the town and lands of Tillimad [Tillymaud] in the parish of Ellone [Ellon]. 
2 CONC [Seal] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD52%2f1714&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1610&di=n National Records of Scotland, Lord Forbes, Lord Forbes, refer
2 CONC ence GD52/1714]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 April 1595: 	Tack by Mr. Edward Bruce, commendator of Kinlos, to William Bruce, his brother, of the small teinds of vicarage of parish of Allane, in sheriffdom of Aberdene, for 19 years. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/n
2 CONC rsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD15%2f880&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1610&di=n National Records of Scotland, Erskine family of Cardross, Perthshire, reference GD15/880]'''
2 CONT
