2 CONT ''' Robert Bruce of Airth'''
2 CONT x Elizabeth Menteith d1521
2 CONT xx  Janet Forrester 
2 CONT *Alexander x Jonet Livingston
2 CONT *John 
2 CONT *Capt.James x Jean/Katheriue Hamilton
2 CONT *William 
2 CONT *NN x Drummond
2 CONT xxx Marion d/o Sir David Bruce
2 CONT *Andrew x Margaret Duddingstone
2 CONT *Robert of Baldrig x Drummond
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert, the eldest son, succeeded his father in Airth 1513, and is mentioned as heir of the deceased Robert Brus of Erth, knight, his father, in 1513 and 1519. He is probably the Robertus de Brus mentioned as one of the Lords of t
2 CONC he Articles, 14 June 1526. He is also mentioned in 1545-46. He resigned a portion of his estate to his eldest son on his marriage in 1547. 
2 CONT Robert Bruce was married three times, 
2 CONT x first to Elizabeth Menteith, who was a widow whose first husband's name was Erskine; she appears to have died in 1521. 
2 CONT xx He married, secondly, Janet, daughter of Sir Walter Forrester of Garden, by whom he had issue four sons and one daughter.
2 CONT xxx His third wife was Marian, daughter of Sir David Bruce, seventh Baron of Clackmannan, and by her he had issue two sons and one daughter. She remarried Magnus Sinclare of Kynninmonth, the second son of William, second Lord Sinc
2 CONC lair, and died July 1575.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children by the second wife were : —
2 CONT
2 CONT >1. Alexander, succeeded his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT >2. John, witnesses numerous deeds.
2 CONT
2 CONT >3. James, Captain Brus, a son of the Lord of Airth, is mentioned as being- taken prisoner at St. Cuthbert's church with ten or twelve horsemen. Captain James was dead in 1613, and married  Jean, or Katheriue Hamilton, and had iss
2 CONC ue two sons, viz. : —
2 CONT
2 CONT >>(1) Alexander, married Margaret Edmistone.
2 CONT
2 CONT >>(2) George
2 CONT
2 CONT >4. William, mentioned in " Bruces and the Cumyns," p. 321. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >5. A daughter, also mentioned in " Bruces and the Cumyns," who married Drummond of Medhope.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of the third marriage were : —
2 CONT
2 CONT >6. Andrew, called of Dysart in "Bruces and the Cumyns," but he certainly was of Nethermongal  or Mongal, for he disponed that property, 10 May 1571, to his brother Alexander Bruce of Airth and his spouse Jonet Livingston ; he mar
2 CONC ried ° Margaret Duddingstone ; they grant a reversion 1572.
2 CONT
2 CONT >7. Robert of Baldrig, witnesses a deed 12 December 1580, and is mentioned  in many transactions ; he was executor to his mother's will and is mentioned as her second son. He married Helen,** daughter of Harrie Drummond, first lai
2 CONC rd of Riccarton.
2 CONT
