2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/572/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 572-3]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/saintclairsofisl00sain/page/301/mode/1up The Saint-Clairs of the Isles: 301-2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>William, fourth Lord Sinclair</strong>, succeeded to the title on the death of his father, but apparently not to the estates until the death of his mother. In 1515 the Orcadians elected Sir James Sinclair, natural son of 
2 CONC Sir William Sinclair of Warsetter, as their leader, withheld the rents due to Lady Sinclair, and forced Lord Sinclair to surrender the Castle of Kirkwall and to flee into Caithness ; but in 1529 he received a letter from the King 
2 CONC instructing him to invade Orkney and deprive Sir James of his usurped governorship. With the assistance of John, Earl of Caithness, he collected a force, landed in Orkney, and encountered the Islesmen at Summerdale, where the Earl
2 CONC  was killed with five hundred of his men, and he himself taken prisoner. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On his own resignation he had a charter of confirmation to him and his spouse Elizabeth Keith of the lands of Newburgh and fishings of Eythan on 17 April 1524, in 1543 he had sasine in the baronies of Dysart and Ravenscraig, and, 
2 CONC on his own resignation, a charter to him and his spouse of the lands of Wiltstoun, Oarberry, and Balbeggy in Fife, on 28 June 1547. 3 He had a remission under the Privy Seal, on 23 October 1542, for assisting George, Lord Home, an
2 CONC d David Home of Wedderburn in their rebellion. In 1544 he signed the agreement to support the authority of the Queen-Mother as Regent against the Earl of Arran. He died in 1570. 5 He married, first, Elizabeth Keith, daughter of Wi
2 CONC lliam, third Earl Marischal, and relict of Colin, Master of Oliphant, and secondly, Mariota Bruce. Issue by first marriage : 
2 CONT * Henry, fifth Lord. 
2 CONT * Margaret.
2 CONT * Barbara. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue by second marriage : 
2 CONT * Magnus, who had a charter of the lands of Kinninmonth in Fife, as son of William, Lord Sinclair, and Mariota Bruce on 14 November 1561, and died at Dysart 16 July 1586. He married Marion, daughter of Sir David Bruce of Clackmann
2 CONC an, and widow of Robert Bruce of Airth. She died in July 1575."
2 CONT * Edward
2 CONT * Hugh
2 CONT * George
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft#page/572/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. VII, page 572
2 CONT
