1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MARY SINCLAIR ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mary Sinclair is identified as the daughter of Lord Sinclair in a number of published genealogies, but the name of her father has not been satisfactorily identified. See [https://archive.org/details/historyofcountyo02pateuoft/p
2 CONC age/119/mode/1up History of the County of Ayr II: 119] and [https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I125255&tree=CC Clan MacFarlane and associated clans genealogy] and [https://www.stir
2 CONC net.com/genie/data/british/cc4rz/cunningham08.php Stirnet: Cunningham 08]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary for William Cunningham of Glengarnock ==
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 - William, who died before his father, married Mary Sinclair [Note], daughter of Lord Sinclair, and had issue :
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Sir James, who succeeded his grandfather.
2 CONT * 2. William of Quarreltoun, who obtained from his father the lands of Quarreltoun, Paisley parish, in 1583.
2 CONT * 3. James, died May 18, 1644.
2 CONT * 4. Jean, married to her cousin, John Schaw of Greenock in 1565.
2 CONT * 5. Andro went to Ireland. Durie, in his Decisions, mentions him as living in 1626
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Identified as 'Mary Sinclair, daughter of Lord Sinclair'. Suggested as being of this generation, and given name suggests by this wife.-Ed.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I125255&tree=CC
2 CONT *[S319] History of the County of Ayr - Vol.'s I & II, James Paterson 1805-1876, (Volume 1 pub 1847 Volume 2 pub 1852), Vol II. 
2 CONT * S6] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Fleming01: The Scots Peerage (Wigtown), Burkes Extinct Pee r ages 1883 (Fleming of Wigtown). 
